course: dictionary
lesson: 9557
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. The word story is a good example. Look at the words around it, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «Headlines are written to grab you, so read the story underneath.» Here a story is a news report, a piece of writing that tells you what really happened. The clue is the headline above it and the word read.
explain: «Each story is 3 metres tall.» In a maths problem about a building, a story is one floor. The clue is the height. A floor is a level, and it is called a storey in British English. A word problem is also called a story problem.
explain: «Don't tell stories» is said to a child who has made something up to cover the truth. Here a story is a lie. The clue is the word tell, and the person being told off. Context tells you which meaning to pick.
fact: A story is something that happens, told in words, pictures or acting. It can be true or made up.
fact: In a news report, «a story» is a piece of news, often under a headline.
fact: In a building, «a story» (British: storey) is one floor or level, so «a 10-story building» has ten floors.
fact: «A story» can also mean a lie told by a child: «Don't tell stories».
fact: To find the right meaning, read the words around the word and try each meaning in the sentence. The one that makes sense is the answer.
exercise: «Headlines are written to grab you, so read the story underneath.» In this sentence, what does story mean? | A lie told by a child | *A news report | A bedtime tale about a bear | A floor of a building
exercise: Maths: «Each story is 3 metres tall.» What does story mean here? | A made-up tale | A news report | A lie | *One floor of a building
exercise: «Theatre is a story told live, right in front of you: the actors are really there.» Find and copy the word that tells you the story is acted, not filmed. | actors | theatre | story | *live
test: Jayden says to his little brother, «Don't tell stories.» What does story mean here? | A news report | *A lie | A tale in a book | A floor of a building
test: «An old Scandinavian folk story said lemmings fell from the sky in storms.» What kind of story is this? | A word problem in maths | A news report from today | *A tale that people told long ago | One floor of a building
exam: «Before passing a story on, check it: a small nip can become a horror story in three tellings.» What does story mean here? | A floor of a building | *A tale that can grow and change each time it is told | A news report that is always true | A lie told only by children
